{"ranking": ["M5", "M6", "M8"], "fault": "M5 (tail current mirror) length was corrupted to 0.15 um. The other mirror devices in the reference family (M6, M8) use L=2.34 um. The short length raises M5's W/L ratio about 15x versus the intended ~4x mirror ratio. M5 tries to sink far more current than it should (~189 uA instead of ~41 uA) and is pushed into triode. Total supply current rises to ~235 uA, giving ~422 uW against a 180 uW limit. Restoring L=2.34 um gives roughly 10 + 41 + 36 uA ≈ 87 uA, or about 156 uW, which meets spec."}
